sequenceDiagram
  participant M as Trusted<br/>management
  participant C as OCC
  participant L as Designated<br/>lifecycle owner
  participant P as Provider
  Note over M,C: Authenticated management caller and admitted purpose<br/>Agent flags and bootstrap delegation cannot select this path
  M->>C: 1. Current authority before access
  Note over M,C: Bind caller / user, tenant, source,<br/>purpose, grant, destination and operation
  C-->>M: Allow, deny or unavailable
  break Denied or authority unavailable
    Note over M,C: Refuse before material access
  end
  M->>L: Request usable material<br/>within original deadline
  Note over L,P: Reuse or prepare through the same lifecycle owner<br/>Owner authorizes its issuer operations
  L->>L: Reuse if eligible<br/>Otherwise coordinated preparation
  Note over M,L: Roots stay confined#59; no second refresher<br/>A failed retrieval may follow a completed refresh
  L-->>M: Usable runtime material + evidence, or failure
  break Failed, withdrawn, unusable or too late
    Note over M,L: Refuse use#59; retain uncertain attempt
    Note over M,L: Reconcile refresh effects#59; no blind replay
  end
  M->>M: Freeze actual operation and material
  M->>C: 2. Fresh authority after preparation
  Note over M,C: Check actual operation, versioned route and grant,<br/>material identity / version#59; no credential bytes
  C-->>M: Allow, deny or unavailable
  alt Allowed, material usable, within original deadline
    M->>P: Inject material#59; send once
    P-->>M: Response or failure
    M->>M: Apply response policy<br/>Return sanitized metadata only
  else Denied, unavailable, unusable or too late
    M->>M: Refuse before provider send
  end
  Note over M,P: No provider tokens or handles to Agent or UI<br/>Each provider operation repeats both checks<br/>No automatic sender retry
